@spec/language.sigil import { SigilWorkspaceConfig }
@packages/cli import { SigilCli }
@integrations/skills/sigil/review-gate.sigil import { SigilReviewGate }
@integrations/skills/sigil/compatibility.sigil import { SigilSkillCompatibility }

component SigilWorkspaceBootstrap {
  goal {
    Establish a compatible configured Sigil workspace and select the appropriate
    greenfield, brownfield, or established-contract workflow before semantic work.
    Keep initialization authority and workspace mutation boundaries explicit.
  }

  interface {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      identifies the target repository and its configuration state before semantic
      workflow selection

      handles configured workspaces, unconfigured repositories with existing Sigil,
      and unconfigured repositories without Sigil

      reports a missing ConfigFile without mutation and initializes only when
      ReviewGate for workspace-initialization returns ready
    }

WorkflowSelection {
      selects Greenfield design, Brownfield adoption, or established-Sigil review
      from implementation and Sigil evidence after workspace bootstrap

      validates ConfigFile and SkillCompatibility before relying on workspace
      semantics
    }
  }
}

expand SigilWorkspaceBootstrap {
  state {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      Configuration state is configured, unconfigured with existing Sigil,
      unconfigured without Sigil, invalid, or outside the selected target.
    }

WorkflowSelection {
      Greenfield applies when no existing implementation constrains the selected
      behavior or component.

      Brownfield applies when relevant implementation exists but Sigil coverage is
      absent, partial, ambiguous, or suspected to have drifted.

      Established-Sigil review applies when the selected boundary already has
      credible contract coverage.
    }
  }

  logic {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      Resolve the selected repository root and any eligible ancestor workspace before
      interpreting Sigil sources.

      When a valid ConfigFile governs the target, validate that configured workspace
      without initialization.

      When no ConfigFile governs the target, inventory existing Sigil paths and
      report the repository as unconfigured without mutation.

      Invoke initialization only when ReviewGate for workspace-initialization returns
      ready.

      When an existing ConfigFile is invalid, preserve it and stop with diagnostics.

      Ask SigilSkillCompatibility to validate the portable skill metadata and
      resolved tool versions. Stop before semantic workflow selection when
      SkillCompatibility fails.
    }

WorkflowSelection {
      Complete WorkspaceBootstrap, then inspect relevant implementation and Sigil
      evidence.

      Select GreenfieldWorkflow, BrownfieldWorkflow, or established-Sigil review from
      that evidence.
    }

GreenfieldWorkflow {
      Begin with the problem, intended users or callers, outcomes, boundaries,
      non-responsibilities, and important constraints.

      Resolve material product, contract, ownership, lifecycle, architecture, risk,
      and verification decisions through DesignConversation.

      Decide whether the project is one bounded area or several before drafting
      components, deriving areas from deployment units, technology boundaries,
      independent reasons to change, shared ownership, and reviewability rather than
      from a fixed list.

      Name each area's directory, module index, and declared-member status, and
      confirm that structure as its own decision before writing any contract.

      Establish the smallest coherent component boundary and draft goal and interface
      before operational detail.

      Run evidence, standards, design compilation, implementation-coverage, and
      concept-identifier review as applicable.

      Write exact scoped Sigil, validate it through DesignCompilationReview, then
      report the written result before implementation review.
    }

BrownfieldWorkflow {
      Use WorkspaceBootstrap and stop boundary inspection while the repository
      remains unconfigured.

      Validate WorkspaceBoundary and inspect the root plus every declared member.

      Gather boundary documentation, manifests, executable configuration, and
      entrypoints.

      Confirm each configured boundary's responsibility, intended outcome, users or
      systems, and external interaction surface.

      Propose and review an ordinary summary component in each boundary's
      ModuleIndexFile.

      After the boundary summary is written and validated through
      DesignCompilationReview, narrow to the requested coherent task boundary and
      reconcile its evidence.

      Write exact task components, expands, locations, and imports, then validate the
      result through DesignCompilationReview.
    }
  }

  constraints {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      Existing Sigil sources without ConfigFile are unconfigured evidence, not an
      established workspace and not a compatibility failure until bootstrap is
      attempted.

      Initialization never overwrites an existing ConfigFile or semantically rewrites
      existing Sigil sources.

      Workflow classification does not determine whether a missing ConfigFile may be
      initialized.

      Review and diagnosis do not initialize an unconfigured repository.

      Workspace initialization requires ReviewGate approval for the exact selected
      repository root and files that may be created.
    }

WorkflowSelection {
      Deterministic facts come from compatible CLI and core behavior.

      Model-assisted judgment, ambiguity resolution, and approval remain
      host-workflow responsibilities.
    }

GreenfieldWorkflow {
      Major product, architecture, persistence, authorization, deployment, and
      lifecycle decisions are not invented silently.

      A module structure is proposed and confirmed before contracts are written,
      because relocating a boundary later moves files and every import naming them.

      A small project remains one boundary until a second area has its own reason to
      change.

      Implementation does not begin until ReviewGate for implementation is ready for
      the validated Sigil and exact implementation scope.
    }

BrownfieldWorkflow {
      ConfigFile initialization never overwrites an existing configuration.

      Configured boundary summaries precede task-specific modeling.

      Additional summary boundaries are not inferred from package manifests or
      directory structure.

      Existing user changes and unrelated dirty-worktree content are preserved.
    }

WorkspaceMutationBoundary {
      CLI and language-server operations do not semantically edit .sigil sources.

      ConfigFile initialization is the narrow CLI mutation exception.

      Semantic Sigil mutation belongs to the written-Sigil design workflow.
    }
  }

  decisions {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      Decision: Keep review and diagnosis bootstrap non-mutating and require
      ReviewGate approval before workspace initialization.

      Scope: Governs repositories without an eligible ConfigFile; excludes validation
      of already configured workspaces.

      Trade-offs: An unconfigured repository requires one explicit initialization
      approval before semantic workspace interpretation.

      Design issues addressed: Automatic initialization contradicted the read-only
      review contract.

      Consequences: Missing configuration is reported without mutation, and
      initialization creates files only after scoped approval.

      Revisit when: The host provides an explicitly authorized initialization mode
      before the Sigil workflow begins.
    }
  }

  cases {
WorkspaceBootstrap {
      An unconfigured repository is inventoried and reported without creating files
      during review or diagnosis.

      Approved workspace-initialization creates only the reviewed ConfigFile and
      optional seeded GlossaryFile.

      An invalid existing ConfigFile is reported without replacement.
    }

WorkflowSelection {
      A component with credible existing Sigil uses established-Sigil review unless
      evidence shows drift.
    }

GreenfieldWorkflow {
      An undecided public behavior discovered during implementation returns to
      DesignConversation and written-Sigil design work.
    }

BrownfieldWorkflow {
      A workspace without ConfigFile is reported as unconfigured before boundary
      inspection and initialized only when ReviewGate for workspace-initialization
      returns ready.
    }

WorkspaceMutationBoundary {
      A read-only validation command reports diagnostics without rewriting Sigil
      sources.
    }
  }
}
